  "disclose": [
    "The released fonts kern with a legacy `kern` table (their GPOS has no kern feature); these sources kern through a GPOS kern feature, which is how fontc builds kerning. HarfBuzz shapes all 1097 kerned pairs of every style alike in both (tools/probes/binary_to_source/results/legacy-kern-pairs.txt in the evidence repository). Decided 2026-10-01: releases with an old kern table are accepted and disclosed.",
    "Sansation Light Italic is flagged italic in the release (fsSelection ITALIC, macStyle italic) with an italic angle of 0, as all of the family's italics are. A Glyphs source cannot state that to fontc 1.0.0, which flags a static font italic only for a nonzero italic angle or a master named Italic or Bold Italic, so the build is flagged regular. Decided 2026-10-02: problems that need fontc are disclosed, and fixed later.",
    "The release's post table names two glyphs of Sansation Light Italic `ffi`; the second, which the f f j ligature substitutes, is `ffi.1` in the source, as fontTools reads it. The table gate, which pairs glyphs by name, therefore compares the release's first `ffi` with the source's and reports its advance (1618 against 1628) as an hmtx difference; the glyph the release draws under that name is unchanged."
  ],
